cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AtlasWM in research, cite this software release and the foundational works listed below."
title: "AtlasWM: Structured Characteristic-Function Regularization for End-to-End JEPA World Models"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-24
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cana"
    given-names: "Darvy"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/darvyc/AtlasWM"
url: "https://github.com/darvyc/AtlasWM"
abstract: >-
  AtlasWM is an end-to-end joint-embedding predictive world model with
  structured characteristic-function regularization. AtlasReg combines
  spherical projection rules, biased and unbiased empirical estimators,
  Gaussian and Student-t targets, exact Gaussian BHEP forms, and multivariate
  subspace objectives for latent distribution matching.
keywords:
  - jepa
  - world-model
  - latent-dynamics
  - characteristic-functions
  - spherical-designs
  - cramer-wold
  - bhep
  - henze-zirkler
